  "strategy": "<ApproachAndRationale>\n    The central idea is to use a continuous optimization approach combined with multi-resolution analysis and bounds enforcement to find a piecewise constant function that minimizes the maximum overlap integral. This differs from the parent algorithm by focusing on:\n\n    1. Smooth function approximation followed by discretization\n    2. Bounded optimization using transformed constraints\n    3. Progressive resolution refinement\n\n    The key limitations are:\n    \u2022 Computational cost for smooth optimization\n    \u2022 Need for gradient-based methods\n    \u2022 Balancing resolution and optimization quality\n\n    This approach aims to escape local optima by leveraging continuous transformations and progressive resolution changes.\n  </ApproachAndRationale>\n\n  <MathematicalSpecification>\n    <Representation>\n      A piecewise constant function h(x) defined on [0,2] with n sample points\n    </Representation>\n\n    <Variables>\n      $h \\in [0,1]^{n}$ with unknown structure\n    </Variables>\n\n    <ExactObjective>\n      $C_5 = \\max_{k \\in [-n+1, n-1]} \\left( \\frac{2}{n} \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h_i (1 - h_{i+k}) \\right)$\n    </ExactObjective>\n\n    <Constraints>\n      $\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h_i = \\frac{n}{2}$\n      $0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\quad \\forall i$\n    </Constraints>\n\n    <SmoothSurrogate>\n      Define transformed variables $d_i = 2h_i - 1$\n      Objective: $C_{\\beta} = \\log(\\cosh(\\beta C_5))$\n      Constraint: $\\sum d_i = 0$\n    </SmoothSurrogate>\n\n    <Method>\n      Bounds-based projected gradient descent\n    </Method>\n  </MathematicalSpecification>\n\n  <ImplementationProcedure>\n    <StepGradientCalculation>\n      <Code>\n        def compute_gradient(h, n):\n          corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")\n          max_corr = np.max(corr) * (2/n)\n          # Approximate gradient via finite differences\n          eps = 1e-6\n          h_plus = np.clip(h + np.eye(n)*eps, 0, 1)\n          h_minus = np.clip(h - np.eye(n)*eps, 0, 1)\n          grad = np.zeros(n)\n          for i in range(n):\n            c_plus = np.max(np.correlate(h_plus[i,:], 1-h_plus[i,:], mode=\"full\")) * (2/n)\n            c_minus = np.max(np.correlate(h_minus[i,:], 1-h_minus[i,:], mode=\"full\")) * (2/n)\n            grad[i] = (c_plus - c_minus)/(2*eps)\n          return grad\n      </Code>\n      <Safety>\n        Uses finite differences with step epsilon=1e-6\n        Clips values to [0,1]\n        Requires correction to maintain constraint\n      </Safety>\n    </StepGradientCalculation>\n\n    <StepProjectedGradient>\n      <Code>\n        def project_feasible(h, n):\n          h = np.array(h, dtype=float).copy()\n  target = n/2.0\n  diff = target - np.sum(h)\n  if abs(diff) < 1e-12: return h\n  factors = 1e-8\n  while abs(diff) > factors:\n    cnt_up, cnt_down = 0, 0\n    for j in range(n):\n      if h[j] < 0.5:\n        cnt_down += 1 if h[j] + (diff/(n*cnt_down+1)) > 0 else 0\n      else:\n        cnt_up += 1 if h[j] - (diff/(n*cnt_up+1)) < 1 else 0\n    if cnt_up + cnt_down == 0:\n      break\n    # Adjust values\n  return h.clip(0,1)\n      </Code>\n    </StepProjectedGradient>\n\n    <StepRun>\n      <Input>\n        seed=budget_s,n_points,initial_h_values\n      </Input>\n      <Steps>\n        parent_resolution = 128\n        if seed == 42 and budget_s > 150:\n            h = np.array(initial_h_values)\n            project_feasible(h, parent_resolution)\n            \n        resolutions = [parent_resolution * 2**i for i in range(3)]\n        t0 = time.time()\n        for n in resolutions:\n            if remaining_time() < 3: break\n            dx = 2.0 / n\n            target_sum = n / 2.0\n            if initial_h_values is None or parent_resolution != n:\n                h = interp_to(initial_h_values, parent_resolution, n)\n                h = project_feasible(h, n)\n            # Use simple gradient descent\n            h_new = h.copy()\n            best_val = compute_c5(h_new)\n            lr = 0.01 * (compute_c5(parent_h) / compute_c5(h))**0.5\n            improvement = True\n            for it in range(200):\n                if remaining_time() < 1: break\n                grad = compute_gradient(h_new, n)\n                origin = h_new.copy()\n                h_new = h_new - lr * grad\n                h_new = project_feasible(h_new, n)\n                val_new = compute_c5(h_new)\n                if val_new < best_val - 1e-10:\n                    best_val = val_new\n                    parent_h = h.copy()\n                    improve_iters += 1\n                else:\n                    h_new = origin\n            parent_h = h_new.copy()\n      </Steps>\n    </StepRun>\n\n    <StepValidation>\n      <Code>\n        final_val = compute_c5(parent_h)\n        valid_parents = np.all((parent_h >= 0) & (parent_h <= 1))\n        finite = np.isfinite(final_val)\n        if not (valid_parents and np.abs(sum(parent_h) - n/2) < 1e-5 and finite):\n            # Fall back to reliable solution\n            parent_h = initial_h_values.copy()\n            parent_h = interp_to(parent_h, len(parent_h), n)\n            parent_h = project_feasible(parent_h, n)\n            final_val = compute_c5(parent_h)\n      </Code>\n    </StepValidation>\n  </ImplementationProcedure>\n\n  <SearchChoices>\n    <Resolutions>\n      Start with 256 samples, then double to 512, then to 512 (max)\n    </Resolutions>\n\n    <LearningRate>\n      Adaptive: lr = 0.01 * (current_objective / initial_objective)'^{0.5}'\n    </LearningRate>\n\n    <Initializations>\n      Use provided initial_h_values when available\n    </Initializations>\n\n    <Feedback>\n      If improvement >= 1e-7, double resolution\n    </Feedback>\n\n    <Variations>\n      Try coordinate descent 20% of the time\n      Alternate between gradient and coordinate descent\n    </Variations>\n  </SearchChoices>\n\n  <ComputeBudget>\n    <Estimate>\n      256 samples: ~0.2 seconds per optimization\n      512 samples: ~0.8 seconds\n      1024 samples: ~2.5 seconds\n    </Estimate>\n\n    <Schedule>\n      Total time allowed: 1300 seconds\n      30% to double resolution (3-4 doublings)\n      70% to optimize current resolution\n      Set timers inside optimization algorithms\n    </Schedule>\n  </ComputeBudget>\n\n  <ValidationAndContract>\n    <Steps>\n      1. $h_i \\in [0,1] everywhere$\n      2. $\\sum h_i = n/2$ within 1e-5$\n      3. Compute C_5 same as reference evaluator\n    </Steps>\n\n    <Fallback>\n      Use initial_h_values if project_feasible fails\n    </Fallback>\n  </ValidationAndContract>",
